course: dictionary
lesson: 8966
title: Sincerely: honest and true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sincerely means honestly and truly, so the person means exactly what they say. «I sincerely hope you feel better» tells the reader that the wish is real, not just polite words.
explain: You will also see sincerely at the end of a letter or email. «Yours sincerely» is used in the UK, Ireland and Australia, and «Sincerely» is used in the US and Canada. Write it just before your name.
explain: In England, use «Yours sincerely» when you know the person's name, as in «Dear Mrs Patel». When you do not know the name, as in «Dear Sir or Madam», use «Yours faithfully» instead.
fact: Sincerely means honestly and truly.
fact: «I sincerely apologise» means you are truly sorry, and you really mean it.
fact: «Yours sincerely» ends a formal letter in the UK, Ireland and Australia; «Sincerely» is used in the US and Canada.
fact: Use «Yours sincerely» when you know the person's name, and «Yours faithfully» when you do not.
fact: Sincerely is on the Years 5–6 word list in England, so practise spelling it: sin-cere-ly.
exercise: «I sincerely hope you feel better.» What does sincerely mean here? | Quickly and loudly | Sadly and slowly | Only sometimes | *Honestly and truly
exercise: You are writing to Mrs Patel, and you know her name. Which ending is correct in the UK? | Love from | *Yours sincerely | See you soon | Bye for now
exercise: Which phrase shows a true, honest apology? | I sort of might say sorry | Oops, my bad, not me | *I sincerely apologise | Whatever, sorry
test: «Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to complain.» Which ending should you use? | See you soon | Yours sincerely | *Yours faithfully | Lots of love
test: Sam writes, «I sincerely thank you for the gift.» What is Sam saying? | Sam is angry about the gift | Sam did not get a gift | Sam is joking about the gift | *Sam truly and honestly means thank you
exam: Which sentence uses sincerely correctly? | *I sincerely hope you can come to my party | Sincerely means very fast and loud | Sincerely the dog ran to the park | The sincerely box is under the bed
